The non-certified ServiceNow integration requires enabling global read access to system event and audit tables, which makes those logs accessible to all applications within the instance—not just AppOmni.
This differs from the certified model, which operates within a scoped application boundary and adheres more closely to least privilege principles.
While the non-certified approach enables enhanced threat detection capabilities, it introduces additional security and compliance considerations, particularly in regulated environments, due to the broader access model and reduced isolation.

